WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.120
Private retrieval-augmented generation, often called private RAG, can help AI systems answer from approved internal material.

2
00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:10.704
It can also create new responsibilities.

3
00:00:10.704 --> 00:00:18.307
Source documents must be ingested, chunked, embedded, indexed, retrieved, cited, updated, expired, and permissioned.

4
00:00:18.307 --> 00:00:24.803
Treating RAG as only a vector database misses the governance work that makes the knowledge trustworthy.

5
00:00:24.803 --> 00:00:28.863
Knowledge control starts with source ownership and provenance.

6
00:00:28.863 --> 00:00:37.130
Teams should know where a document came from, who owns it, when it was ingested, what version it represents, and whether it is current.

7
00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:47.317
Metadata matters because the AI system may retrieve fragments without the original context that humans normally use to judge authority, audience, and freshness.

8
00:00:47.317 --> 00:00:49.679
Permissions must survive retrieval.

9
00:00:49.679 --> 00:00:56.323
A user should not receive content through an AI answer that they could not access through the source system.

10
00:00:56.323 --> 00:01:04.074
Tenant boundaries, document-level permissions, collection-level permissions, and query-time enforcement all matter.

11
00:01:04.074 --> 00:01:09.463
It is not enough to protect the storage location if retrieval ignores the access rules.

12
00:01:09.463 --> 00:01:12.637
RAG quality also depends on lifecycle discipline.

13
00:01:12.637 --> 00:01:15.220
Old guidance can be retrieved as current.

14
00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:17.656
Chunks can lose important qualifiers.

15
00:01:17.656 --> 00:01:20.461
Conflicting sources can appear side by side.

16
00:01:20.461 --> 00:01:23.783
Sensitive documents can enter the wrong collection.

17
00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:33.232
A sovereign AI program needs reviewable ingestion, retrieval testing, source citations where appropriate, expiration rules, and update workflows.

18
00:01:33.232 --> 00:01:41.426
Retrieved text is context and evidence; it should not be treated as unlimited authority over policy, law, or operational judgment.
